  "criterion": "GATE6 end-to-end clone-reset rehearsal on real dogfood workspace byte-clones",
  "recorded_interpretation": "The live dogfood engine.db is TypeScript-authored and the Rust fence correctly refuses its foreign fingerprint. The authorized cutover is a reset: retain the source SQLite files inside the byte clone, initialize and bind a fresh Rust store in the clone, write the two harness-only markers, then exercise run_rehearsal(NoFaults). Ice accepted the data wipe; this interpretation remains flagged for Ice's post-hoc review.",
  "floor_clone_design_decision": "The byte clone applies the canonical capture floor to both directory roots and files, except the .dohc subtree required by the rehearsal machinery. Reset never touches capture-excluded content because it is outside the engine's world. Every omitted root or file is recorded, and the complete contents of omitted directory trees are independently hashed into the before/after source proof. Alias and special-file refusal remains fail-closed for every entry actually cloned.",
